{"tool_name":"cell-or-particle-counting-and-scoring-stained-objects-using-cellprofiler","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>This is a Jupyter notebook demonstrating the run of a code from IDR data sets by loading a <a href=\"http://biii.eu/cell-or-particle-counting-and-scoring-percentage-stained-objects\">CellProfiler Pipeline&nbsp;</a></p>\n\n<p>The example here is applied on real data set, but does not correspond to a biological question. It aims to demonstrate how to create a jupyter notebook to process online plates hosted in the IDR.</p>\n\n<p>It reads the plate images from the IDR.</p>\n\n<p>It loads the CellProfiler Pipeline and replace the reading modules used to read local files from this defaults pipeline by module allowing to read data remotely accessible.</p>\n\n<p>It creates a CSV file and displays it in the notebook.</p>\n\n<p>It makes some plot with Matplotlib.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>This is a Jupyter notebook demonstrating the run of a code from IDR data sets by loading a <a href=\"http://biii.eu/cell-or-particle-counting-and-scoring-percentage-stained-objects\">CellProfiler Pipeline&nbsp;</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The example here is applied on real data set, but does not correspond to a biological question. It aims to demonstrate how to create a jupyter notebook to process online plates hosted in the IDR.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It reads the plate images from the IDR.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It loads the CellProfiler Pipeline and replace the reading modules used to read local files from this defaults pipeline by module allowing to read data remotely accessible.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It creates a CSV file and displays it in the notebook.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It makes some plot with Matplotlib.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2018-10-18T15:35:57+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2018-08-16T11:11:50+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":t